      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carter_Lake%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the 1930s and ’40s, Carter Lake became a gambling hub, with venues like the Chez Paree offering horse‑race betting and prime‑rib meals.",
